  "holdout_note": "Organism strings are UniProt's OS= spelling, verified against the reference index. A holdout that removes nothing raises rather than running, which is how nine wrong names in the first draft were found. SARS-CoV holds out 'Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus', which also removes SARS-CoV-2: stricter than intended, kept.",
  "segmented_note": "A segmented genome is supplied as every segment, comma-joined. Three entries named only one segment in the first draft: Hantaan gave S alone and could yield only the nucleoprotein, so two of its three labels were unmatchable by construction; Lassa gave S alone, missing the L-segment polymerase; CCHF gave M alone. A label naming a protein the supplied genome cannot encode marks the ranker wrong for a gene that was never in the input.",
  "unscoreable_note": "An instance with fewer candidates than labels cannot be informative, and one with no identified candidate cannot be scored at all. Human parvovirus B19 returns 8 ORFs and zero identified chains, so it has no ranking to score; it is a finding about reach, not a panel error, and belongs in its own tier rather than in a recall denominator."
